## Code Conventions

- **TypeScript**: strict mode, no `any`, interfaces. Details in `.claude/rules/typescript.md`
- **Tests**: 80%+ coverage, no mocks except external deps, edge cases. Details in `.claude/rules/testing.md`
- **Security**: validate inputs, escape outputs, parameterized queries. Details in `.claude/rules/security.md`
- **Naming**: camelCase (vars/functions), PascalCase (classes/components), SCREAMING_SNAKE (constants), kebab-case (files)

### Secrets management

- IMPORTANT: Never commit secrets (.env, credentials, API keys)
- Use environment variables

## Default Happy Path (Semantic Routing)

Any request without an explicit slash command automatically benefits from the repo context injected by the `UserPromptSubmit` hook (`scripts/hooks/prompt-context.sh`). This context hints a routing to `/assistant-auto`.

- Trivial intent (< 50 LOC, 1-3 files) → `/work:work-quick`
- Standard feature / bugfix → `/work:work-flow-feature` or `/work:work-flow-bugfix`

Disable: `SKIP_PROMPT_CONTEXT=1`.

